pace consistency, coverage, and source-label deletion audits; ...   * connectivity-aware `7:2:1` split validation with no validation/test NaN cells; ...     git clone https://github.com/NKU-DOIE/OdorNet.git\n## Baseline Training\n\nBaseline training does not require the Zenodo archive. The baseline notebook uses the processed train, validation, and test CSV files already included in this GitHub repository:\n\n  * `notebooks/odornet_baseline_training.ipynb`: fixed-split baseline training following the reference notebook's MolFormer fine-tuning and simple GCN/GNN baselines under Drop, Union, and Intersection missing-label policies.\n\n## Technical Validation Notebook\n\n`notebooks/technical_validation.ipynb` is the single public notebook for the technical-validation workflow. It contains:\n\n  * SEA construction from descriptor statistics, expert correction, and AI-assisted semantic alignment;\n  * label-space consistency, coverage, and source-label deletion audits;\n  * RDKit cleaning and canonical structure checks;\n  * connectivity-aware `7:2:1` split validation with no validation/test NaN cells;\n  * raw multi-dataset comparisons and Drop/Union/Intersection training;\n  * publication-oriented result and training-curve visualizations.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - akashnathai/multi-structure-liver-ct: Simultaneous liver, tumour, and hepatic-vessel segmentation from CT using anatomical-constraint losses and connectivity-aware (soft-clDice) learning. · GitHub (https://github.com/akashnathai/multi-structure-liver-ct)\nciteturn77search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; 🌿 Connectivity-aware vessel learning — a differentiable soft clDice (centerline-Dice) loss so the predicted vessel tree stays topologically connected, plus connectivity metrics (clDice, connected-components error, centerline overlap) for evaluation.\n\n  1. akashnathai\n  2. multi-structure-liver-ct\n\n## Repository navigation\n\n  *   *